<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad al-Muzaffar of Badajoz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1045–<a href="/years/1068">1068</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad al-Muzaffar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a> was the second Aftasid ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Badajoz, reigning from about 1045 to 1068. He fought long wars with the Taifa of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> and lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coimbra">Coimbra</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-leon">Ferdinand I of León</a> in 1064, paying him tribute. A learned man, he compiled a vast anthology known after him as al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kitob">Kitab</a> al-Muzaffari.</p></div>
